========================================================================================================
FEE EXPERIMENT — amount block widened to admit A down to 5% BELOW B (asymmetric)
========================================================================================================

  Baseline block: |A - B| <= 0.01, symmetric.
  Widened block:  that, OR  0.95*|B| <= |A| <= |B|  with matching sign.
  Asymmetric because a fee reduces the settled amount and never inflates it.
  This is ONE setting, reported as-is. The width was not tuned.
  The classifier is still the frozen BenchRec-train model — now applied over a
  candidate set built differently from the one it was fitted on, which is a
  second domain shift on top of the synthetic one.

